{"id": "EUVD-2026-108736", "enisaUuid": "f7ed3ce1-ab2d-3379-a3f0-4c0e8c979034", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: do not warn on route notification size race\n\nfib6_info_hw_flags_set() sizes the skb with rt6_nlmsg_size() and later\nfills it with rt6_fill_node().  With nexthop compatibility mode enabled,\na concurrent replacement can grow the group between these independent\nsnapshots.  rt6_fill_node() can then legitimately return -EMSGSIZE, so\nthe warning does not prove a sizing bug.\n\nRemove the warning.  The existing error path still frees the skb and\nreports the error to listeners.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a3b935b6b6037eefb36bd27a60793a008358e8d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b112bd43f1172fb152e848570a957467008a5ae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ac7d92a4698e34e614c254359665b9de1f65283", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/291fe0bafee78c95f9f2e7f579f17793fd5a1e5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c97426ec649d99596d8969e1a052c16b14b7b485"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99070"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d2b99c7-1d46-33d9-8da6-a1526e2de66f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "907eea486888cfe118c19759bbc4b8fca2e004df <291fe0bafee78c95f9f2e7f579f17793fd5a1e5a"}, {"id": "3120df54-aa2d-30ce-9bc6-924fd0ef2d3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}, {"id": "408fdeed-075b-35c1-b18c-579865144f9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "5743fa01-1830-3493-8548-94255b6aea23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5a013568-e43c-3aa3-a358-dfd3733f0dc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5e663de6-7800-3a91-b896-8c29702073f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "907eea486888cfe118c19759bbc4b8fca2e004df <4ac7d92a4698e34e614c254359665b9de1f65283"}, {"id": "6ba23c2b-743c-31db-a251-d0d9fed92ce5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "907eea486888cfe118c19759bbc4b8fca2e004df <7b112bd43f1172fb152e848570a957467008a5ae"}, {"id": "6bbd1ec3-df1a-3aca-b32b-10a71295376f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "907eea486888cfe118c19759bbc4b8fca2e004df <c97426ec649d99596d8969e1a052c16b14b7b485"}, {"id": "742797ac-6a6b-320a-b53d-083a43afc1f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "907eea486888cfe118c19759bbc4b8fca2e004df <8a3b935b6b6037eefb36bd27a60793a008358e8d"}, {"id": "81e28de1-3c12-391e-a369-1eabca1a5aeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "bf750bc8-14aa-3ff6-a4e8-a352862da12a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "efcb631b-e4f8-310f-ab6d-80bd3ac0a11f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3a6f1b43-9d35-3a0a-a892-3b485b685019", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}